  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A ball with a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> collides with another identical ball at rest. After the collision, the direction of each ball makes an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with the original direction. If the ratio of velocities of the balls after the collision is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>y</mi></math>, then what is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/22c82fd2-d64a-4ee5-8e60-1d0b86590954-image.png\" style=\"width: 274px; height: 171px;\" /></p><p>From conservation of momentum along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>",
